  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Intangible Cultural Heritage and Developing Cultural Tourism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is aiming towards the development of 10 cultural tourism destinations in the 4 districts of Jodhpur, Jaisalmer, Barmer and Bikaner involving 1500 traditional performing artists and handicraft artisans. It will result in the safeguarding of ICH, increased footfall at the artists&apos; villages, and increased average days of stay by visitors. This will lead to the promotion of cultural tourism based on music and craft traditions with an aim of benefitting artists&apos; communities, recognition for the villages and artists and new income opportunities for the tradition bearers as well as the larger community.</narrative>
  </description>
